{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Interpretation 1</b><br>אפך. The nose." "<b>Interpretation 2</b><br>צוארך כמגדל השן. White." "And after he likened her eyes to pools, for they are broad, he likened the nose [to a tower] which is even, without crookedness." "<b>Interpretation 3</b><br>צוארך. The heads of the host." "עיניך. The prophets who were at first few in number, now they shall be many." "(אפך. He is the High Priest) as in the matter of \"they shall place incense in your nose\" — (Numbers 19:18, the word אפך here understood as \"before you\")."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {5 "Ibn Ezra reads אפך as 'before you' connecting it to Numbers 19:18 where the same form means 'before you'; but the bracketed note 'the High Priest' suggests a separate interpretation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:54.175327683Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}